From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: the generic locale model takes C.UTF-8 as C

The generic model, which libstdc++ uses with C libraries other than
glibc, supports only the "C" locale, and std::locale("") throws
"locale::facet::_S_create_c_locale name not valid" when LANG names any
other.  Systems on musl name C.UTF-8 there, the C locale with UTF-8
characters, so every program calling std::locale("") on them threw (PR
libstdc++/15992 for the general case).  The model's facets use the C
library, whose own LC_CTYPE gives the encoding, so C.UTF-8 and C.utf8
are taken as C; other names still throw.

libstdc++-v3/ChangeLog:

	* config/locale/generic/c_locale.cc
	(locale::facet::_S_create_c_locale): Accept "C.UTF-8" and
	"C.utf8".
	* testsuite/22_locale/locale/cons/c_utf8.cc: New test.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/libstdc++-v3/config/locale/generic/c_locale.cc b/libstdc++-v3/config/locale/generic/c_locale.cc
--- a/libstdc++-v3/config/locale/generic/c_locale.cc
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/config/locale/generic/c_locale.cc
@@ -239,10 +239,13 @@
   locale::facet::_S_create_c_locale(__c_locale& __cloc, const char* __s,
 				    __c_locale)
   {
-    // Currently, the generic model only supports the "C" locale.
+    // Currently, the generic model only supports the "C" locale.  It
+    // takes "C.UTF-8", the C locale with UTF-8 characters, which systems
+    // on C libraries such as musl name in LANG, as the same: its facets
+    // use the C library, whose own LC_CTYPE gives the encoding.
     // See http://gcc.gnu.org/ml/libstdc++/2003-02/msg00345.html
     __cloc = 0;
-    if (strcmp(__s, "C"))
+    if (strcmp(__s, "C") && strcmp(__s, "C.UTF-8") && strcmp(__s, "C.utf8"))
       __throw_runtime_error(__N("locale::facet::_S_create_c_locale "
 			    "name not valid"));
   }
diff --git a/libstdc++-v3/testsuite/22_locale/locale/cons/c_utf8.cc b/libstdc++-v3/testsuite/22_locale/locale/cons/c_utf8.cc
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/testsuite/22_locale/locale/cons/c_utf8.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
